  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Toyota Tacoma?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. The DIMO LTE R1 reports a fuel level signal in liters, which you query through the Telemetry API. To detect refuels, use the segments query with the refuel detection mechanism, which flags where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Toyota Tacoma with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. After the vehicle is shared with you, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the vehicle's signals through the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Toyota Tacoma?",
      "a": "Use the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling detection mechanism, which requires a DIMO device. Idle segments are contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range, and you can adjust the upper bound with the maxIdleRpm setting (default 1000)."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Toyota Tacoma mileage?",
      "a": "A DIMO device reports the odometer signal in km. To get verifiable proof of the reading, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the resulting credential through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Toyota Tacoma, 2010 and newer model years connect through a DIMO device, and this coverage is tested rather than expected. Once a vehicle is shared with you, you can query it through the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance."
